  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the RDA is <strong>0.8&nbsp;g per kg</strong> of body weight (0.36&nbsp;g per lb). Active people do better with <strong>1.2&ndash;1.6&nbsp;g/kg</strong>, and <strong>1.6&ndash;2.2&nbsp;g/kg</strong> (0.7&ndash;1&nbsp;g per lb) to build muscle. For a 170&nbsp;lb person that is about 62&nbsp;g (RDA) to 170&nbsp;g.</p></div>

